# Public FormSubmit AJAX configuration, embedded in browser output by Vite.
# Format: https://formsubmit.co/ajax/{anonymous-token}
# Use only the invisible-email random alias obtained after owner activation.
# The token is public; never substitute a recipient address or API/archive key.
# Tokens must be 16–128 letters, digits, hyphens, or underscores; no URL extras.
# Leave blank until activated. Blank disables the only public contact method
# and blocks release. No real token or recipient is supplied in this repository.
# Set this variable in the Amplify main branch environment, then rebuild.
# Activation, deployment, and a live QA submission require separate authorization.
# Confirm private receipt before release readiness. No conventional account needed.
# VITE_FORM_KEY and other unsupported public variables remain rejected.
VITE_FORM_ENDPOINT=

# Public monitoring metadata. Leave all blank until the shared Master Planning
# organization and the cobalt-web project have been verified. No credentials here.
# Enabled only on the canonical production host; see docs/monitoring.md.
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=
VITE_SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT=
VITE_SENTRY_RELEASE=

# Set these private build variables in the existing CI secret/configuration store,
# never with VITE_ prefixes and never in committed files:
# SENTRY_ORG, SENTRY_ORG_ID, SENTRY_PROJECT=cobalt-web, SENTRY_PROJECT_ID,
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN, SENTRY_UPLOAD_SOURCEMAPS=true.
# Use a separately named Cobalt upload credential; never another repo's token.
